        {
            "sub_event_index": 1,
            "place_index": 4,
            "PlaceName": "la Haye-du-Puits",
            "Sub-event_summary": "The VIII Corps is designated to lead the U.S. First Army offensive southward along the Cotentin west coast, aiming to advance twenty miles to secure high ground near Coutances and form a new army line to Caumont. The plan involves sequential attacks by adjacent corps, with VIII Corps facilitating the advance by threatening enemy flanks. The corps targets key terrain around la Haye-du-Puits, including hills and ridges, using three divisions in a V-shaped thrust, with specific objectives assigned to each division, and plans for the 8th Division to replace the 82d Airborne.",
            "Event_Doc": "chapter4a-event.json",
